      agentNote:
        "Free-text answers go through a small model (gpt-oss-20b, Groq's free tier), which only picks among the dataset's options; the server checks its pick. Without it, the browser's rules take over. Only the final profile goes to the pipeline.",
      agentName: 'Intake agent',
      agentOn: 'gpt-oss-20b · Groq',
      agentOff: 'rules only',
      agentOffTitle: "The model didn't answer right now; the browser's rules keep reading the answers.",
      thinking: 'reading the answer',
      srcOption: 'option',
      srcRules: 'rules',
      srcLlm: 'gpt-oss-20b',
      allOptions: 'see all options',
      question: 'question',
      fxTitle: 'Why reais, if the data is German?',
      fxBadge: 'R$ 9.70 per DM',
      fxText:
        "credit-g comes from a 1970s German bank, with amounts in Deutsche Marks (DM). Before training, mlops-platform converts the dataset to Brazilian reais at R$ 9.70 per DM: the amount is multiplied by the rate and the balance and savings brackets become R$ brackets (DM 200 becomes R$ 1,940). The model was retrained that way and only knows reais. The rate is by purchasing power: €1 = DM 1.95583 (fixed parity), German prices rose about 3.25× since 1975 and the euro is near R$ 5.85. Changing the scale doesn't change what the model learns: the AUC is the same as the Deutsche Mark version.",
      formCurrency: 'R$',
      pipeTitle: 'The pipeline, step by step',
      pipeHint: 'The steps take about 100 ms on the server; the page shows one at a time, with the time measured there.',
      onServer: 'on the server',
